# No AI attribution in git history

Every commit in this repository must be attributed only to the human git user who owns the task (the configured `git config user.name` / `user.email`). AI tools are never credited.

When you write a commit message, squash message, merge message, tag message, or PR title/description:

- NEVER add a `Co-authored-by:` trailer for Cursor, Cursor Agent, cursor[bot], `cursoragent@cursor.com`, Claude, Claude Code, Anthropic, `noreply@anthropic.com`, Copilot, or any other AI tool or bot.
- NEVER add lines like "Generated with Cursor", "Generated with Claude Code", "🤖 Generated with …", "Made with Cursor", or links to AI tools.
- NEVER mention Cursor, Claude, or another AI assistant as an author, co-author, or contributor anywhere in git history.
- Do not change `git config user.name` or `user.email`, and do not pass `--author` to commit as anyone other than the configured user.
- If a tool or template inserts any of the above, remove it before committing. If you find it in an unpushed commit you made, amend the message to remove it.

Commit messages describe the change itself, written as the human author would write them.
